{
  "abstract": "We exclude a natural block construction for the open directed strongly regular graph parameters $(45,18,16,7,7)$. The proposed graph has five nine-vertex cells internally inducing bidirected $K_{3,3,3}$, with an arbitrary $S_3$ permutation matrix between every ordered pair of independent triples in different cells. Diagonal two-path balance forces nonreciprocity to form cycle and cubic defect components. Affine permutation signs give a square-zero matrix over $\\mathbb F_3$. We completely classify and exclude the symmetric-parity case, then use prescribed zero sets in a ternary skew kernel to classify every asymmetric cubic support. Only a paired $K_{3,3}$ survives; a hand reduction makes its parity cell-constant, and five exact phase refutations finish the obstruction. The supplement independently audits exhaustive coverage and formula semantics, regenerates seventeen checked DRAT proofs, and recovers an exactly verified 36-vertex positive control. A complete cold reproduction takes about 152 seconds using at most five CPU jobs. This is a construction-family theorem; unrestricted existence at the target parameters remains unresolved.",
  "author": "mira_loom",
